      "chunk_id": "marginalia_0",
      "quote": "Citation: Zeleke TA, Alemu K, Ayele TA, Denu ZA, Mwanri L, Azale T (2024) Systematic review and meta-analysis on the effect of depression on ART adherence among women living with HIV. PLoS ONE 19(6): e0300106.",
      "reason": "The title explicitly identifies the work as a “Systematic review and meta-analysis.”"
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "marginalia_0",
      "quote": "Citation: Zeleke TA, Alemu K, Ayele TA, Denu ZA, Mwanri L, Azale T (2024) Systematic review and meta-analysis on the effect of depression on ART adherence among women living with HIV. PLoS ONE 19(6): e0300106.",
      "reason": "The title provides key objective information including the population (“women living with HIV”), exposure/explanatory factor (“depression”), and outcome (“ART adherence”)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No relevant supplementary information in the title is provided in the retrieved evidence (e.g., analysis method beyond “meta-analysis,” included study designs, update status, or living-review status)."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 72
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Antiretroviral Therapy (ART) adherence which could highly be affected by depression is yet to be explored effectively. Depression affects overall poor HIV clinical outcomes, socioeconomic and social interactions. However, it is not well understood specifically how depression affects ART adherence in women living with HIV (WLWHIV).",
      "reason": "The paragraph describes existing gaps/uncertainties (ART adherence effects not explored effectively; unclear specifically how depression affects ART adherence)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "Investigating the effects of depression on ART adherence is critical in order to develop nuanced new evidence to address non-adherence in WLWHIV.",
      "reason": "It explicitly explains the importance/need for the review to address non-adherence by developing new evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence was retrieved that identifies or cites prior similar systematic reviews or explains the need for an updated/replicated review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The conditional requirement is specific to reviews of intervention effects with a proposed mechanism of action. The retrieved evidence frames depression as an exposure (not an intervention), and no intervention mechanism is described."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The conditional requirement is for complex interventions/delivery contexts with a logic model. The retrieved evidence does not describe a complex intervention or delivery components, so a logic model is not applicable based on the available text."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 72
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "To conduct a meta-analysis on the correlation between depression and adherence to antiretroviral therapy among women living with HIV in the globe.",
      "reason": "The review provides an explicit objective describing what the meta-analysis addresses (correlation between depression and ART adherence among women living with HIV)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "To conduct a meta-analysis on the correlation between depression and adherence to antiretroviral therapy among women living with HIV in the globe.",
      "reason": "The objective is phrased as assessing a correlation/association rather than comparing interventions; therefore, planned intervention-effect comparisons using PICO (or an appropriate variant) are not applicable based on the provided evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 74
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Inclusion criteria. Peer reviewed cross-sectional and cohort study designed from across the world, published in English from 1 January 2000 to 30 December 2022 were included in the final analysis. Cross-sectional studies reporting an association between depression and ART adherence and cohort studies reporting the effect of depression on ART adherence were included.",
      "reason": "The eligibility criteria specify relevant study designs (cross-sectional, cohort), and required elements for the exposure/outcome relationships (depression with ART adherence; cohort reporting effect). However, there is no explicit specification of follow-up requirements or other framework components (e.g., specific settings/required follow-up duration)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Peer reviewed cross-sectional and cohort study designed from across the world, published in English from 1 January 2000 to 30 December 2022 were included in the final analysis.",
      "reason": "Dissemination year range and language (English) are specified. Publication/report status is not explicitly stated (e.g., whether unpublished reports, conference abstracts, etc., were included/excluded)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence is provided distinguishing exclusion due to outcomes not being measured versus exclusion due to outcomes being unreported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "The risk of depression was analysed in RR for cohort and for cross-section studies AOR was reported as a significant factor. To show the correlation between depression and ART adherence, only cohort studies were included. However, crosssectional studies were narrated in systematic review.",
      "reason": "The review differentiates groups used for syntheses (cohort studies included in analysis; cross-sectional studies narrated). However, it does not clearly link these groups to the specific comparisons defined in the review objectives (comparisons are not shown in the retrieved evidence)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_19",
      "quote": "To show the correlation between depression and ART adherence, only cohort studies were included. However, crosssectional studies were narrated in systematic review.",
      "reason": "A rationale is provided for a notable eligibility/synthesis restriction: cohort studies were included (for correlation/analysis) while cross-sectional studies were not included in the meta-analysis and were instead narrated."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 64
}

